('EN7-Q02',['mass-confusion'],'Accepted lower Confusion has a native d4 behavior table, independent direction/target draws, one hard admission and actual regular-start opportunities.','A: expressly reuse that complete finite native table and bridges in this new source, with new same-name replacement policy specified. B: infer a global random-behavior rule or add external confusion/double attacks.','Recommend explicit A. Show all table entries, unavailable-budget/target/no-safe-path outcomes, perception-qualified target sets and stable draw identity. No reroll-until-harmful, forced finite resources, extra turns or hidden target list. Decide coexistence with lower Confusion and other instructions by actual arbitration. Five Fate presentation entries stay unchanged; another behavior table is not automatically a disclosed sixth presentation.'),
('EN7-Q03',['dominate-greater-beast'],'Printed magical beastsCR12orlower,range120,concentration1minute. Lower Dominate Beast is actual Beast/INTsave60.','A: authoritative native magical-beast classification plus actual CR<=12. B: infer eligibility from magical appearance, a spell-created body, any Beast/Monstrosity or guessed CR.','Recommend A and identify required catalog fields. PreserveCR12 ceiling and120range. If no full authoritative qualifying record exists, declare the future positive case conditional; authoring a profile is a separate explicit content decision. A transformed character does not acquire monsterCR by analogy.'),
('EN7-Q04',['dominate-greater-beast'],'Source control lacks precise commands/saves; actual lower Beast and higher Person have different repeat saves and same-source coexistence.','A: explicitly select initial save, repeat-save/harm ending and replacement policy, with ordinary action/movement instruction limits. B: silently mix favorable fields from both counterparts.','Recommend a complete local choice, including same-plane conscious mental order delivery and no remote senses/secret disclosure. Retain actual native ordinary attack sequence but no compelled spellcasting/finite expenditures. Bind future regular-start and owner-attached execution separately, one actual remaining budget and shared admission, no unwilling owner BA. Eligibility may be application-only only if expressly selected.'),
('EN7-Q05',['mindfog-field'],'Area causes-2toINT/WIS/CHAchecksANDsaves; CoreAction120Instantaneous.','A: choose fixed finite zone, lifetime/concentration and actual recipient eligibility with first-exposure history. B: name implies physical fog/obscurement, reduced ability scores or automatic saveDC/RP changes.','Recommend A. Choose radius/height, initial save or no-save, entry/cover-return behavior, all-creatures versus enemy-only and whether penalties apply only during active exposure. Preserve all six roll categories. An initial resistance save should resolve before an unestablished penalty unless a new rule explicitly says otherwise.'),
('EN7-Q06',['mindfog-field'],'Same-named overlapping zones and roll snapshots can multiply penalties or leak hidden zones.','A: strongest identical-penalty application while independently retaining each record/clock/exposure result. B: unbounded-2stacking or suppressing a losing source deletes it.','Recommend A as an expressly chosen source-local stacking policy. Actual INT/WIS/CHA ability checks and saves only, not attacks/DC/passive score by thematic inference; if passive check conversion is intended, author it explicitly. Choose whether a committed roll snapshots before or after a legal interrupt changes exposure. No private source diagnostics in player-facing failure output.'),
('EN7-Q07',['lasting-control'],'Extend ALL current Enchantment spells10minutes; Action120; this spell itself requires concentration1minute. Ordinary commitment ends own incompatible concentration before payload.','A: snapshot eligible existing effects after actual payment/concentration replacement, including only expressly chosen ownership/range locus. B: snapshot before payment and resurrect the caster’s ended concentration.','Recommend A. The printed all must cover every qualifying effect within the selected scope, not just one. Explicitly resolve whose spells, actual school used, caster-origin versus effect/recipient range and LoE. Other casters’ concentration is not automatically ended by this caster committing. An expired prior own spell cannot be revived as an extension target.'),
('EN7-Q08',['lasting-control'],'Printed+600seconds outlasts this spell’s maximum60seconds; bounded-control and original deadlines normally do not renew.','A: explicitly authorize one finite+600s amendment to eligible live spell duration, with defined persistence when Lasting Control ends. B: temporary maintenance overlay that vanishes with its own concentration, or another complete finite model.','Director must select and reconcile the source promise. State exact extension of elapsed clocks versus typed regular-turn endpoints, effect concentration ownership and maximum, derivative rider clocks, and genuine exception to prior nonrenewable control. No ability to reopen spent hard-control admission, already completed effects, one-shot orders, consumed charges or expired targets. Do not silently claim ordinary control policy already authorizes ten extra minutes.'),
('EN7-Q09',['lasting-control'],'Recasting and copying could make indefinite control chains. Source says all current spells, including potential earlier Lasting Control.','A: explicit one-extension-per-original-spell lifetime cap and exclude extension-only modifiers from recursive amplification. B: cumulative extensions with some other explicit finite ceiling.','Recommend A as a substantial NEW limit for Director decision. Track original application ID across copied sources, suppression, replacement and initiative transitions; no rest/controller change refunds it. Resolve instantaneous/permanent/ended/suppressed spells individually. A multiclass owner’s non-Enchantment casting mode is not eligible merely because an alternate placement is Enchantment.'),
('EN7-Q10',['power-word-pain'],'One target with100HPorless; CoreAction120InstantaneousVSF. Title does not provide no-save, Verbal-only or pain anatomy immunity.','A: after legal paid commitment check actual current normalHP<=100, excluding independenttempHP, then selected initial resistance. B: free preflight displays hiddenHP or condition name grants physiology immunity.','Recommend A as a new completion; actual form uses same current HP unless an explicit source says otherwise. State whether unconscious/living/nonliving targets qualify by exact chosen native rule. Failed hidden eligibility is nondiagnostic. Do not remove S/F or automatically kill/damage/inflictWound.'),
('EN7-Q11',['power-word-pain'],'Crippling pain supplies no exact penalties, clock or healing endpoint.','A: finite explicit soft penalties and/or separately admitted hard component, with exact repeat save and ending. B: import an external penalty list or grant total action denial without admission.','Request a complete native consequence profile. If it includes Speed/action/spell restrictions, identify each independent component and defenses. Decide whether rising above100afterestablishment ends it or whether threshold was application-only. Healing/removal must have actual named authority; no new permanent injury or reset of control history on recast.'),
('EN7-Q12',['project-image'],'Two placements: Enchantment120remote duplicate with sightANDhearing; IllusionSelfduplicate of caster. Current class access maps all actual eligible classes to Enchantment.','A: preserve both source profiles but use actual acquisition/class-school access, with Illusion comparison retained ungranted unless a real permitted route exists. B: merge Self/120and both functions or grant Wizard free alternate school.','Recommend A. Return complete distinct profile decisions or an explicit justified harmonization that preserves both source promises, not silent access expansion. Choose finite duration/concentration, exact initial placement and size. No creature HP, inventory, physical collision body, independent turn, spell origin or teleport follows from an image.'),
('EN7-Q13',['project-image'],'Enchantment sightANDhearing needs simultaneous remote sensory and control procedure; generating source is not automatically Divination.','A: explicit ordinary sight/hearing from the image, source-qualified senses/Blindness/Deafened and finite control/movement/tether. B: infer omniscience, arbitrary plane viewing, sensory targeting through wards or whole-body manifestation.','Recommend A with exact Action costs for moving/switching/maintaining, whether local senses replace/supplement, and legal remote target permission limited to what real spell origins permit. Define how image motion traverses solid walls or remains within LoE; intangible appearance alone does not grant unbounded remote mapping. Protection from Scrying applies by actual generating classification, not theme. No record/replay/database access or voice credential authorization.'),
('EN7-Q14',['project-image'],'Appearance interaction and disbelief/suppression can accidentally grant a diagnostic target.','A: noncreature image with specified visual/auditory/physical-interaction handling and each actual suppression locus. B: let every creature-targeted attack/removal apply or expose hidden observer result globally.','Recommend source-local rules including disbelieving observer’s effect and retained other viewers. Clarify whether it can emit caster speech or sounds; seeing/hearing through it does not print speech transmission. Same source clock continues when suppressed; return gives no replayed information or new image. Preserve physical/source-observer private information boundaries.'),
('EN7-Q15',['reverse-gravity'],'Both placements print creaturesANDobjects50ftradius,Actionrange50,concentration1minute,VS M-or-F.','A: finite explicitly selected 3D field with upward falling, actual detached objects/cargo/body eligibility and no whole-structure detachment. B: omitobjects or lift whole dungeon through partial intersection.','Recommend A with exact height, origin, surface boundary and eligibility. Specify anchored/bolted/carried/melded items, partial-body intersection and object fixed-world support. No invented common density, structuralHP or breaking force; require actual authored object profiles. Preserve objects as real matter and original container/gear relationships.'),
('EN7-Q16',['reverse-gravity'],'Upward fall then field exit/ceiling/ending involves actual falling timing, flight, anchors, collision and suppression.','A: explicit finite upward-fall source using actual distances and timing, then ordinary falling once eligible gravity returns. B: free teleport, oscillating infinite boundary damage or arbitrary stop-in-air.','Require exact top-boundary behavior, initial legal grasp/save opportunity, maintained grip/flight and collision/fall damage source. An outside anchor must be physically reachable with real anatomy and support. Choose what field-center suppression versus local clipped region does; no duplicate movement history or replay on reentry. Use real occupied volumes, current velocity treatment if modeled and actual fall schedule; do not infer terrain simulation already exists.'),
